Deserializing seqs with elements in arbitrary order

I am writing a deserializer for a format, and in this format, you can have structs inside structs, and these are always sequences/allow multiple copies. A problem I have run into is when the order these inner structs show up in isn't contiguous/sorted. So when I have
```
outer "Outer" {
    inner1 "First" {
    }
    inner1 "Second" {
    }
    inner2 "Third" {
    }
    inner2 "Fourth" {
    }
}
```
I do fine, because my seq deserializer just keeps going until `inner1` changes to something else (or I encounter '}'), and then calls it a day. But if the file instead looks like this:
```
outer "Outer" {
    inner1 "First" {
    }
    inner2 "Third" {
    }
    inner1 "Second" {
    }
    inner2 "Fourth" {
    }
}
```
I'm in trouble, because the second time I come across `inner1` and try to deserialize it again, serde tells me
> duplicate field `inner1`

Is there some way for me to tell serde to combine the sequences instead of considering them duplicates? Because I parse as I go, I can't know that another value from a previous sequence will come up until I'm already at the point where I'm deserializing the "same seq" twice.

