If I have nested parallel loop, how can I change number of threads of inner parallel loop?

I have a function `f` that uses Rayon's parallel iterator to parallelize heavy computing. I want to run this `f` with different parameters in parallel. This scenario is very often like hyperparameter search in Machine Learning.

Here is a simple example code of the above case. 

```rust
use rayon::prelude::*;
use std::{thread, time::Duration};

fn dummy_func(i: usize) -> usize {
    println!("started {}", i);
    let duration = Duration::from_secs(1);
    (0..4).into_par_iter().for_each(|_| thread::sleep(duration));
    println!("ended {}", i);
    i
}

fn main() {
    let mut res = vec![];
    (0..100)
        .into_par_iter()
        .map(|i| dummy_func(i))
        .collect_into_vec(&mut res);
    dbg!(res);
}
```

If the range of outer loop is large enough, turning off parallelization of the inner loop is preferred.  Now I want to know how I can dynamically change parallelization level of the inner loop function `dummy_func`. Shall I create a dedicated threadpool each time I call `dummy_func` ?

```rust

fn main() {
    let mut res = vec![];
    (0..100)
        .into_par_iter()
        .map(|i| {
            let pool = rayon::ThreadPoolBuilder::new()
                .num_threads(1)
                .build()
                .unwrap();
            pool.install(|| dummy_func(i))
        })
        .collect_into_vec(&mut res);
    dbg!(res);
}
```

