gl_vertexID variable from converting from wgsl to glsl vertex shader received in naga, which is not compilable by wgpu

When I try to convert the vertex part of the example wgsl shader from [learn wgpu tutorial](https://sotrh.github.io/learn-wgpu/beginner/tutorial3-pipeline/#writing-the-shaders) through Naga, I got this
```
#version 450 core
struct VertexOutput {
    vec4 clip_position;
    vec4 color;
};
layout(location = 0) smooth out vec4 _vs2fs_location0;

void main() {
    uint in_vertex_index = uint(gl_VertexID);
    VertexOutput out_ = VertexOutput(vec4(0.0), vec4(0.0));
    float x = (float((1 - int(in_vertex_index))) * 0.5);
    float y = (float(((int((in_vertex_index & 1u)) * 2) - 1)) * 0.5);
    out_.clip_position = vec4(x, y, 0.0, 1.0);
    vec4 _e24 = out_.clip_position;
    out_.color = _e24;
    VertexOutput _e25 = out_;
    gl_Position = _e25.clip_position;
    _vs2fs_location0 = _e25.color;
    gl_Position.yz = vec2(-gl_Position.y, gl_Position.z * 2.0 - gl_Position.w);
    return;
}


```
which seems fine, except gl_vertexID is not a valid token that can be read by naga. And this cannot be passed through `wgpu` to be converted into valid draw call, as, well `gl_VertexID` according to the source code, is not valid, while `gl_VertexIndex` is. 
So i am not sure if this is a rendering side of an issue from wgpu? or a compiling side issue from naga. But this is quite strange to me.
this is the error message
```
thread 'main' panicked at 'called `Result::unwrap()` on an `Err` value: [Error { kind: UnknownVariable("gl_VertexID"), meta: Span { start: 185, end: 196 
} }]',
```
Even if I try to use gl_VertexIndex in my own shader code, it still seems to fail, I don't know why.
here is the proof of concept vertex shader
```
#version 450
layout(location = 0) out vec3 frag_color;
void main(){
    vec2 pos[3] = vec2[3]( vec2(-0.7, 0.7),
                           vec2(0.7, 0.7),
                           vec2(0.0, -0.7) );
    gl_Position = vec4( pos[uint(gl_VertexIndex)], 0.0, 1.0 );
    frag_color = color;
}
```
fragment shader
```
#version 450
layout(location = 0) in vec3 frag_color;
