RAM usage is incorrect in v1.12.1

encountered

## Current Behavior

## Steps to Reproduce

1. deploy a 3 node cluster, each node has 6 cpu cores and 512MB ram
2.create a collection, config is below
```
{
  "result": {
    "status": "yellow",
    "optimizer_status": "ok",
    "indexed_vectors_count": 120211,
    "points_count": 134604,
    "segments_count": 18,
    "config": {
      "params": {
        "vectors": {
          "size": 768,
          "distance": "Dot",
          "on_disk": true
        },
        "shard_number": 9,
        "replication_factor": 2,
        "write_consistency_factor": 1,
        "on_disk_payload": true
      },
      "hnsw_config": {
        "m": 16,
        "ef_construct": 128,
        "full_scan_threshold": 10,
        "max_indexing_threads": 3,
        "on_disk": false
      },
      "optimizer_config": {
        "deleted_threshold": 0.05,
        "vacuum_min_vector_number": 500,
        "default_segment_number": 2,
        "max_segment_size": null,
        "memmap_threshold": 7000,
        "indexing_threshold": 10000,
        "flush_interval_sec": 10,
        "max_optimization_threads": 2
      },
      "wal_config": {
        "wal_capacity_mb": 32,
        "wal_segments_ahead": 0
      },
      "quantization_config": {
        "scalar": {
          "type": "int8",
          "quantile": 0.99,
          "always_ram": true
        }
      },
      "strict_mode_config": {
        "enabled": false
      }
    },
    "payload_schema": {
      "to_user_id": {
        "data_type": "keyword",
        "points": 134604
      },
      "from_user_id": {
        "data_type": "keyword",
        "points": 134604
      },
      "time_id": {
        "data_type": "integer",
        "points": 134604
      }
    }
  },
  "status": "ok",
  "time": 0.02574141
}
```

3. insert random generated points continously, until one of these pod OOM

## Expected Behavior

RAM usage in every pod is 130k * 768dim * 1bytes(int8) * 2(replicas) / 3 = 62MB, mainly the quantization costs
But actually RAM usage is over 512MB and then pod encountered OOM crash

## Possible Solution

It seems like vectors are all stored in RAM, not disk, even the config value `vectors.on_disk` is `true`

If vectors and quantizations are all store in RAM, it will cost
130k * 768dim * 5bytes(int8 quantization + float32 vector) * 2(replicas) / 3 = 328MB for every pod

## Context (Environment)

## Detailed Description

use the version v1.12.1

## Possible Implementation

