#[sea_orm::model]
#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, DeriveEntityModel, Serialize, Deserialize)]
#[sea_orm(table_name = "change_change")]
pub struct Model {
    #[sea_orm(primary_key)]
    pub id: u64,
    #[sea_orm(has_one)]
    pub child_set1_a: HasOne<Child>,
    #[sea_orm(has_one)]
    pub child_set1_b: HasOne<Child>,
}
```

But this causes a compile error, **"Within a single entity, the same model can only be used once with `has_one`!"**

I've searched through all available issues and tried every possible solution—including consulting various AI assistants—but nothing works. Is it really impossible for SeaORM to support this kind of structure?

I suspect the reason is that `Related` can only be implemented once:

```rust
impl Related<super::child::Entity> for Entity {
    fn to() -> RelationDef {
        super::child::Relation::BakeryManager.def()
    }

    fn via() -> Option<RelationDef> {
        None
    }
}
```

