Reopening: in https://github.com/rust-lang/miri/pull/992, CI failed because a bump in a crate, together with not having a lockfile, means Miri doesn't build on CI any more (the new version of compiletest-rs does not work with old nightlies any more). And until https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/65342 lands we also will be unable to make it build again, so Miri development is just halting until that situation is resolved.

That's quite awful, and having a lockfile would avoid this kind of situation.

@ehuss is there any way to have a lockfile here in the Miri repo in a way that when the same file appears in the rustc tree (due to it being a submodule), it does not cause trouble for cargo?

