With the following implementation already existing for Response:
```
impl Response<Body> {
    /// Take the `Body` of this response.
    #[inline]
    pub fn body(mut self) -> Body {
        self.body.take().unwrap_or(Body::empty())
    }
}
```

Would this make more sense?
```
impl<B> Request<B> {...
    /// Read the Request body.
    #[inline]
    pub fn body_ref(&self) -> Option<&B> { self.body.as_ref() }
...}

impl Request<Body> {
    /// Take the Request body.
    #[inline]
    pub fn body(self) -> Body { self.body.unwrap_or_default() }
}
```

My only concern with returning a default is that I think the caller should be able to identify if a body exists or not, but `body_ref()` seems to cover that use case.

Also, should I change the above impl for Response to use `self` instead of `mut self` so it consumes the response? Or should I leave it as-is? This would reduce the differences further.

